<h2 id="-why-i-blog">📝 Why I Blog</h2>

<p>Blogging grew out of the evolution of how I store knowledge:</p>

<p><strong>Stack → Heap → References → Keyword Index → Blog</strong></p>

<p>At first my brain was an empty stack, pushing knowledge in until stack overflow; switching to heap storage, I ran out of <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Out_of_memory">memory</a>; then I tried reference-tag storage, until my browser tabs multiplied like a virus; finally I kept only keywords to search with, only to find many articles had been deleted by their authors. Meanwhile I had my own technical experience worth sharing, so I decided to start this blog.</p>

<blockquote>
  <p>Even if my views are full of narrow theories and naive arguments, I’ll keep doing it, knowing today is right where yesterday was wrong. Otherwise I’d regret the wasted years and be ashamed of accomplishing nothing.</p>
</blockquote>

<p>Blogging keeps me calm and focused on my own field, away from restlessness. I share technology and life occasionally, without obsessing over quality — after all, I also need to spend time working and living well.</p>

